[17592186421979 1079 #uuid "dbcc53b2-5f84-54cb-ad5c-a16cf94b1669" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421937 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421949 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421952 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421955 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421958 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1077 "selection" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421958 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421980 1079 #uuid "e996cded-d3ba-5d9b-afa2-4b9d6ae9a669" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421938 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421941 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421964 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421968 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421971 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1077 "selection" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421964 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421981 1079 #uuid "f16f7ac3-5d3e-5fdc-9751-952a50dea70c" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421940 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421945 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421954 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421961 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421963 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1077 "selection" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421961 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421982 1079 #uuid "f267f788-271e-50ed-b945-f7aa83b94fe5" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421983 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421977 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421983 1069 "q-130755" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421983 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421983 1071 "A fair coin is tossed $20$ times. What is the mean number of tails that occur?" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421983 1072 #uuid "25a0a850-41a7-52c6-b901-d7ad5795dcd0" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421983 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of tails that occur. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ tosses\n\n- since the coin is fair, the probability of landing on tails for each toss is $p=\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of tails that occur is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(20)(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421984 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421974 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421984 1069 "q-130763" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421984 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421984 1071 "There are $15$ gift boxes in a lucky gift machine, $6$ of which have a toy inside. After being picked, the gift box will be replaced by another one of the same value. Six kids are waiting in line for their turn to use it. What is the variance of the number of kids who get a toy?" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421984 1072 #uuid "35949c7a-955a-5bb4-ba6f-41e4641f0ce2" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421984 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of kids who get a toy from the $6$ kids.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=6$ kids that are waiting in line for their turn to use the machine\n\n- since there are $6$ toys out of a total of $15$ gift boxes, then the probability that a kid gets a toy is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{6}{15}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{2}{5}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of kids who get a toy is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (1-\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421985 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421982 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421985 1069 "q-84745" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421985 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421985 1071 "A fair eight-sided die is rolled $6$ times. What is the mean number of times that the outcome of a single roll is either $2,5,$ or $7?$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421985 1072 #uuid "4a15eeec-0407-53e4-9770-0d33f30c6d02" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421985 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times a $2$ or $5$ or $7$ is rolled.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=6$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a $2,5,$ or $7$ on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{3}{8}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of times we get a $2$ or a $5$ or a $7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421986 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421980 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421986 1069 "q-130764" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421986 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421986 1071 "A  fair octahedral die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $8$ is rolled $25$ times. What is the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3?$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421986 1072 #uuid "5f3fbaf6-b15b-53c6-9279-fcc77fd83e0b" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421986 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of times we get a number divisible by $3.$\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=25$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a number divisible by $3$ (i.e., a $3$ or a $6$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(25,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{75}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421987 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421981 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421987 1069 "q-130752" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421987 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421987 1071 "A tennis player has a $60%$ chance of winning each match in a $5$-match tournament. What is the mean number of matches that the player wins?" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421987 1072 #uuid "9f3bf9f8-8f58-5a26-b354-f87af2b2eaa9" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421987 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of matches that the player wins.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=5$ matches\n\n- the probability of winning each match is $p=60%=0.6$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.6).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of matches that the player wins is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(5)(0.60) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421988 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421976 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421988 1069 "q-89408" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421988 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421988 1071 "A student answers a multiple-choice test choosing each answer at random. If the test has $20$ questions, and each question has $4$ possible answers with only one correct answer, what is the variance of the number of correct answers?" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421988 1072 #uuid "afe30003-2595-50a2-8b60-8382c78a5f23" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421988 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of correct answers.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ questions\n\n- the probability of selecting the correct answer in each question is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of correct answers is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421989 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421975 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421989 1069 "q-130883" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421989 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421989 1071 "An infectious flu virus is spreading through a school. The probability of a randomly selected student having the flu next week is $0.2.$ If a class has $23$ students, what is the standard deviation of the number of students having the flu next week? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421989 1072 #uuid "cd4098b0-44f3-5628-89ab-3a85dd72d97e" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421989 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of students having the flu next week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=23$ students in the class\n\n- the probability of selecting a student having the flu next week is $0.2$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(23,0.2).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of students having the flu next week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(23)(0.2)(1-0.2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(23)(0.2)(0.8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3.68} \\\\  & ≈1.918\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421990 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421979 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421990 1069 "q-130766" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421990 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421990 1071 "A new drug has a $64%$ probability of curing a patient within a week. If $50$ patients are treated, what is the standard deviation of the number of cured patients within a week? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421990 1072 #uuid "e3dde14a-c77b-5290-8e8d-52f3133ef7aa" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421990 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of cured patients within a week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=50$ patients in the sample\n\n- the probability that the new drug has cured a patient within a week is $p=64%=0.64$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(50,0.64).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of cured patients within a week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(50)(0.64)(1-0.64)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(50)(0.64)(0.36)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11.52} \\\\  & ≈3.394\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421991 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421978 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421991 1069 "q-84691" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421991 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421991 1071 "An archer practices shooting $16$ arrows at a target. The archer has a $25%$ chance of hitting the bull's eye. What is the variance in the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye?" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421991 1072 #uuid "ed91a13d-0a09-59c4-bf60-d5ad7aad9e5f" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true] [17592186421991 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=16$ shots\n\n- the probability of hitting the bull's eye for each arrow is $p=25%=0.25$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(16,0.25).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of arrows hitting the bull's eye is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(16)(0.25)(1-0.25) \\\\  & =(4)(0.75) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-06c51642-996d-5135-870c-db34a80b53f0" 17592186421929 "answer-07cebf32-de57-5ac9-b739-e5dd0c9c0388" 17592186421930 "answer-0a1da0bd-fbca-576c-9d98-2c5457624d78" 17592186421931 "answer-0e4bdfc2-c0e9-5af4-abe8-067d3285da99" 17592186421932 "answer-12e44cce-8bca-5ac8-80a0-02abd7b3acd2" 17592186421933 "answer-155de04a-19c5-548a-9a38-8b17697942c4" 17592186421934 "answer-162e61c6-2672-53bc-b506-42b887c80bb5" 17592186421935 "answer-1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" 17592186421936 "answer-22e19085-b196-5d51-9863-47908156eca8" 17592186421937 "answer-25cf9ed6-5d80-5316-a85f-81ae68ce439d" 17592186421938 "answer-2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" 17592186421939 "answer-2fec556e-e148-5b1e-97a7-c14be487a96c" 17592186421940 "answer-33ea5317-6dc1-5052-854f-8321410625d5" 17592186421941 "answer-34b2a832-8cee-5042-b5f3-310a15c0aa97" 17592186421942 "answer-396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" 17592186421943 "answer-3f592e8f-e602-59d7-9c67-f601dddbe2e4" 17592186421944 "answer-4124268c-a67c-5426-94fd-b3b803fb7198" 1759218642